topics.description:
A **media query** applies CSS only when a condition is true. It is the base of responsive design.

### Syntax
```css
@media (min-width: 768px) { ... }          /* classic */
@media (width >= 768px) { ... }            /* range syntax (modern) */
@media (width < 600px) { ... }
@media (min-width: 600px) and (max-width: 900px) { ... }
@media screen and (orientation: landscape) { ... }
@media print { ... }
```

### Common features
| Feature | Example |
|---|---|
| `width` / `height` | viewport size |
| `orientation` | `portrait` / `landscape` |
| `prefers-color-scheme` | `dark` / `light` |
| `prefers-reduced-motion` | `reduce` |
| `hover` and `pointer` | `(hover: hover)`, `(pointer: coarse)` for touch |
| `resolution` | `(min-resolution: 2dppx)` retina |

### Choosing breakpoints
Do not chase specific devices. Add a breakpoint **where your content breaks**. Typical references: 480, 768, 1024, 1280 px. The final project in this course steps down at 1400, 1220, 1100, 998 and 768px using `@media (width <= 998px)`.

### Combining
Comma means OR: `@media (width < 600px), print { }`. Use `not` and `and` for more logic.

### @supports - feature queries
Check if the browser understands a declaration:

```css
.gallery { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; }
@supports (display: grid) {
  .gallery { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
}
@supports not (aspect-ratio: 1) { .box { padding-top: 100%; } }
```

### Tip
Keep media queries close to the component (nesting helps) instead of one giant block at the bottom.

examples.css:
body { font-family: sans-serif; }
.cols { display: grid; gap: 10px; grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
.cols div { background: #2965f1; color: #fff; padding: 20px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px; }
@media (width >= 420px) { .cols { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
@media (width < 420px) { .hint { color: crimson; } }

.box { padding: 20px; border: 3px solid #0f172a; background: #fff; color: #0f172a; font-family: sans-serif; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { .box { background: #0f172a; color: #fff; border-color: #fff; } }
@media (hover: hover) { .box:hover { background: #fde68a; color: #000; } }
@supports (display: grid) { .box { display: grid; place-items: center; min-height: 100px; } }

.layout { display: grid; gap: 10px; font-family: sans-serif; }
.c { background: linear-gradient(135deg,#6a11cb,#2575fc); color: #fff; padding: 22px; text-align: center; border-radius: 10px; }
@media (min-width: 380px) { .layout { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
@media (min-width: 560px) { .layout { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); } }

.bar { display: flex; font-family: sans-serif; color: #fff; }
aside { width: 240px; background: #451952; padding: 16px; }
main { width: calc(100% - 240px); background: #ae445a; padding: 16px; }

topics.description:
Media queries react to the **viewport**. **Container queries** react to the size of a **parent container**, so a component adapts to wherever it is placed (sidebar, main column, modal).

### Step 1: declare a container
```css
.card-wrap {
  container-type: inline-size;     /* track width */
  container-name: card;            /* optional */
}
/* shorthand */
.card-wrap { container: card / inline-size; }
```

### Step 2: query it
```css
@container card (width <= 600px) {
  .card { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
}
@container (min-width: 400px) { ... }
```

The queried element must be a **descendant** of the container (a container cannot style itself).

### Container query units
`cqw`, `cqh`, `cqi`, `cqb`, `cqmin`, `cqmax` - 1% of the container's size. Great for fluid type inside cards: `font-size: clamp(1rem, 5cqi, 2rem);`.

### Container vs media query
| | Media query | Container query |
|---|---|---|
| Reacts to | viewport | nearest container |
| Best for | page-level layout | reusable components |
| Same component in two places | same look | can look different |

### Notes
- `container-type: inline-size` applies containment, so the container cannot size itself from its children's width.
- Style queries (`@container style(--theme: dark)`) exist for custom properties.
- The source demo used a bordered box and compared `@container changelayout (width <= 600px)` to a plain media query.

examples.css:
body { font-family: sans-serif; }
.wide, .narrow { container-type: inline-size; border: 3px solid #ffb000; margin-bottom: 12px; padding: 8px; }
.wide { width: 100%; } .narrow { width: 220px; }
.card { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 90px 1fr; gap: 10px; align-items: center; }
.img { background: #2965f1; color: #fff; height: 70px; display: grid; place-items: center; }
@container (width < 320px) {
  .card { grid-template-columns: 1fr; text-align: center; }
  h3 { color: #e11d48; }
}
